the grid border, and may also extend right to the border.\n- Every column of the rectangle may extend up to the border, and may also extend down to the border.\n\n**Which stripes appear.** A stripe is drawn only when its path from the rectangle to the border holds no marker. If a marker lies anywhere on that path, the whole stripe on that side is skipped. The opposite side of the same row or column is judged on its own.\n\nChecking this against pair 1 (rectangle rows 5–9, columns 4–8):\n- **Right:** rows 6, 7 and 9 extend. Row 5 has a marker at x=12 and row 8 has one at x=13, so neither extends. Row 7 still extends right even though it has a marker at x=1, because that marker is on the left.\n- **Left:** rows 5, 6, 8 and 9 extend. Row 7 is blocked by its marker at x=1.\n- **Up:** only columns 5 and 7 extend. Columns 4, 6 and 8 have markers above the rectangle.\n- **Down:** columns 4, 6 and 7 extend. Column 5 has a marker at y=16 and column 8 has one at y=13.\n\nThe output matches this exactly. Pairs 2 and 3 work the same way. In pair 3, row 4 is blocked on the left by the marker at (4,2), but it still extends right. The diagonal \"segments\" listed in the fact sheet are just where these stripes happen to meet, not separate features.\n\n**Test input.** The rectangle covers rows 2–8 and columns 9–15.\n- **Left:** rows 2, 4 and 7 are blocked by markers at x=6, x=5 and x=1. Rows 3, 5, 6 and 8 extend to x=0.\n- **Right:** rows 3 and 8 are blocked by markers at x=19. Rows 2, 4, 5, 6 and 7 extend to x=19.\n- **Up:** nothing above the rectangle, so all seven columns extend up to y=0.\n- **Down:** columns 9, 13 and 15 are blocked by markers at y=12, 17 and 19. Columns 10, 11, 12 and 14 extend to the bottom.\n\n**Construction stages.** The program fills the stripes one side at a time and emits a canvas after each side (left, right, up, down). It then emits the finished grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    rect = max(objs, key=lambda o: o[\"size\"])\n    c = rect[\"colour\"]\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = rect[\"box\"]\n    H, W = g.shape\n    orig = g.copy()\n\n    # left\n    for y in range(y0, y1 + 1):\n        if np.all(orig[y, :x0] == bg):\n            g[y, :x0] = c\n    emit(g, \"Extend each rectangle row to the left border unless a marker lies on that path.\")\n    # right\n    for y in range(y0, y1 + 1):\n        if np.all(orig[y, x1 + 1:] == bg):\n            g[y, x1 + 1:] = c\n    emit(g, \"Extend each rectangle row to the right border unless a marker blocks it.\")\n    # up\n    for x in range(x0, x1 + 1):\n        if np.all(orig[:y0, x] == bg):\n            g[:y0, x] = c\n    emit(g, \"Extend each rectangle column up to the top border unless a marker blocks it.\")\n    # down\n    for x in range(x0, x1 + 1):\n        if np.all(orig[y1 + 1:, x] == bg):\n            g[y1 + 1:, x] = c\n    emit(g, \"Extend each rectangle column down to the bottom border unless a marker blocks it.\")\n    emit(g, \"Final grid: unblocked stripes drawn on all four sides, markers unchanged.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"paths":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Which stripes appear.** A stripe is drawn only when its path from the rectangle to the border holds no marker."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"If a marker lies anywhere on that path, the whole stripe on that side is skipped."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Extend each rectangle row to the left border unless a marker lies on that path."}],"rays":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The rectangle shoots straight stripes outward from its four sides, and each stripe is one row or one column wide."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Every row of the rectangle may extend left to the grid border, and may also extend right to the border."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Every column of the rectangle may extend up to the border, and may also extend down to the border."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"ec694652029d263442cdb1bb2e24c0dc13ebcec1ba19b5f763dc07c89996e736","task_sha256":"ec50a23203594715f396098227a60bd61f8dca67fa8bb14d1a9ab6e5b5ad64c1","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
